  "claim": "A self-contained note (LaTeX, 5 pages) for outside readers, with an independent replay: for every radius r a periodic tiling by the pinwheel triangle has all its patches of tile radius r in pinwheel tilings (the rhombus lattice cut once has every collar a pinwheel collar; each further cut defeats a larger radius), so the pinwheel tilings have no undecorated local rules; the collar rule forces one level of composition and no more; labels read from a bounded window never help, and of the 1,024 decorated substitutions on one bit per tile 1,022 admit a periodic plane, one (with its relabelling) being open.",
